{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/528223-demon-blooded-and-demonic-form","id":528223,"title":"Demon-Blooded and Demonic Form","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-25T16:56:36-07:00","id":528223,"title":"Demon-Blooded and Demonic Form","content":"Howdy!<br /> <br /> So, quick question for you all. I've finally had the time to dig into Demon: the Descent, and Heirs to Hell and am LOVING both of them, however, I was wondering if anyone had seen any way within the rules for a demon-blooded to acquire either Demon Form or something similar to it?<br /> <br /> I noticed the &quot;Terrible Form&quot; merit, and I suppose with some tinkering a demon-blood version would be possible, but I am fully willing to admit I am NOT familiar enough with GMC as a system to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6154-deathmonkee","name":"DeathMonkee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T19:44:52-07:00","id":528415,"title":"","content":"Flowers of Hell (the Demon Player's Guide) details that it's possible to remove and graft demonic form parts onto another Demon and has proper mechanics for that.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> Re-reading the rules for it, a Demon can create a gadget that contains one of its Demonic Form abilities. Such a Gadget can be used as an isolated device with the Demonic form ability's function, but other Demons can graft the gadget onto themselves. They even have their own independent stockpile of Aether, so it stands to reason that you can graft them into humans.<br /> <br /> The mechanics for this are in Flowers of Hell, Pg 158-161","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","user":"Xenesis","date":".  Found the real rules. 05-25-2015, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T20:21:43-07:00","id":528443,"title":"","content":"Thank you!<br /> <br /> Hmmmmm, very intereeeeeeeeesting.<br /> <br /> Reading through it looks like this would be one way for a demon-blooded to be able to hold more than 5 Aether at once, because they would be able to access the store inside the graft, and able to re-fill it too, if I'm reading that right.<br /> <br /> Now the question becomes, what is the limit on grafts? And what stops there from being a <i>Samuel Haight</i> Fractal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6154-deathmonkee","name":"DeathMonkee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T22:11:08-07:00","id":528541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathMonkee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/528223-demon-blooded-and-demonic-form?p=528443#post528443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what stops there from being a <i>Samuel Haight</i> Fractal?</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that form gadgets exist by the will of their donors, persist at their sufferance, and can be violently detonated and reclaimed for the cost of a burner Cover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T22:32:26-07:00","id":528551,"title":"","content":"Very true, indeed that does make it something that someone on their own would not be able to easily pull off......however. The book does hint that it is unknown what happens to grafts after the demon that they came from is dead, as well as mentions a black market for gadgets(pg 160 Flowers of Hell, bottom left). It also mentions a group that has been stealing body parts from dead angels and making grafts from them.(same page of Flowers of Hell)<br /> <br /> Given that all of that, I could see doing up the stats for a Fractal that has been stealing body parts from angels, and has a graft from a dead parent that started him on his clinically insane body part snatching ways. He would make a great antagonist, especially if you had him making pacts with Infernal demons left and right the closer the players got to him.<br /> <br /> Then after he is dead, if they are demons, his whole body is loot!...........yeah, thats kinda morbid..........","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6154-deathmonkee","name":"DeathMonkee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T22:55:09-07:00","id":528562,"title":"","content":"Mind, there <i>is</i> fairly open ground for this sort of particular shenanigan with demonic backing \u2014 &quot;make humans more like demons&quot; is explicitly a subtype of Hell, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T22:58:04-07:00","id":528564,"title":"","content":"Rumors of nephilim being in the Storyteller's Guide abounds, as an aside. WHo knows what they're like, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T23:15:57-07:00","id":528576,"title":"","content":"Hmmmm, nephilim eh? Intriguing! Now I find myself curious!<br /> <br /> On a slightly more serious note though, I'm actually kinda surprised that the Fractals don't have some sort of alternate &quot;demonic form&quot; they can go into, what with them being to quote the book,<br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">In mathematics, a fractal is a pattern that is identical<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> or nearly identical at every scale.</span></span></span></span>&quot; and &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">In Unchained parlance,<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> Fractals are the extraordinarily rare progeny of two demons<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> and, as children go, they fit Mandelbrot\u2019s description of<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> fractals perfectly. They are a beautiful mingling of human<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> flesh with the intuitive mastery of the laws of arcane physics<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> that marks demons.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>&quot;<br /> <br /> So with the above description, why don't they have some sort of alternate form or at least the potential for one at the upper most levels of power?<br /> <br /> Has anyone attempted to write any sort of merit giving them access to a demonic form of their own that anyone has noticed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6154-deathmonkee","name":"DeathMonkee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T23:24:46-07:00","id":528581,"title":"","content":"They already have the ultimate power, and a power that even Demons themselves do not have!<br /> <br /> They're the only things in the nWOD who actually can tell when a Demon is lying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T23:26:37-07:00","id":528583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathMonkee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/528223-demon-blooded-and-demonic-form?p=528576#post528576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So with the above description, why don't they have some sort of alternate form or at least the potential for one at the upper most levels of power?</div> </div> </div> </div>Innate facility with the arcane laws of Embeds is less of an embuggerance of the &quot;identical at every scale&quot; descriptor than an aspect of existence that relies on the wave-particle duality of being a quantum uncertainty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Has anyone attempted to write any sort of merit giving them access to a demonic form of their own that anyone has noticed? </div> </div> </div>I've got a highly situational thing whose subjects can barely be called demon-blooded anymore, but that's for a personal project and relies on a quirk of metaphysical location besides.<br /> <br /> A lambda keyed off of Merge and/or Terrible Avatar may be a more conventional way to do it, as might a Merit with Sleeve Integrator as a prerequisite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T23:37:48-07:00","id":528603,"title":"","content":"In heirs of hell, it mentions that demon-blooded and their demonic parents can become entangled, so that say if the demon burns the cover that was the parent another cover will be the parent.<br /> <br /> Well, that offers lots of options. What if the demon only had an animal, object, ghost, or spirit cover left? What if the Demon didn't have any covers left and was stuck in demon form?<br /> <br /> You could have a demon-blooded character that as far as reality is concerned, is the child of a demon in all their biomechanical glory.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T00:33:18-07:00","id":528620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Originally posted by <b>Satchel</b><br /> ......as might a Merit with Sleeve Integrator as a prerequisite. </div> </div> </div>Now that sounds like an interesting idea, and I would love a writeup of that if someone would be interested in devoting a few minutes to do it. I don't even know where to start, unless it was just a small merit that gave the host access to a few Modifications?<br /> <br /> So, looking over all the suggestions related to grafts I can see that it has all kinds of ways of getting really out of hand, and blowing up the character is going to feel like a really heavy handed way of dealing with it. So I thought that I might take a crack at coming up with a quick hack at a &quot;Terrible Form&quot; Merit for Demon-Blooded. This is what I got so far for that:<br /> <br /> Demonic Form(3-5, Style)<br /> Requirement: Fractal<br /> Effect: Your demonic nature has chosen to manifest itself more strongly than most and you have discovered that you now have a demonic form not unlike that of your parent.<br /> At three dots your demonic form has only two Modifications.<br /> At four dots you have one Technology as well.<br /> At five dots, you also have a single Propulsion.<br /> <br /> Your Demonic Form is more limited than that of your parent in that you are unable to &quot;Go Loud&quot;. Shape Shifting costs 1 Aether both ways(into and out of), and is an instant action. It lasts for one scene. You heal 1 point of bashing or lethal damage from changing shape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6154-deathmonkee","name":"DeathMonkee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}